# Research Harness — template for local secrets, contacts and runtime config.
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill the values:  cp .env.example .env
#
# H8: keys live ONLY in environment variables; config files store variable
# NAMES only, never values. Leave a line blank to keep that value `unknown`
# (H7: a blank never becomes a plausible guess).
#
# `.env` loading into rh is wired in M2-01. Until then, export manually:
#     set -a; source .env; set +a
#
# Exact auth requirements per adapter/provider are verified and recorded in
# their card (docstring + PR: verified-vs-assumed). Notes here are a guide.

# =========================================================================
# 1. Runtime control (RH_*) — not secrets. Usually left unset (defaults).
# =========================================================================
# Host adapter. Default: claude-code. (Codex host lands in M3-16.)
RH_HOST=
# UI language for rh messages: uk | en. Default resolution: --lang > RH_LANG
# > author profile > uk.
RH_LANG=
# NOTE: RH_AGENT_SESSION=1 is set automatically by the host shell (Claude
#   Code via .claude/settings.json) — do NOT set it by hand.
# NOTE: RH_TEST_MODE / RH_FAULT_AT / RH_FAULT_KILL / clock override are
#   test-harness internals (02 §11). Never set them in a real .env.

# =========================================================================
# 2. Source APIs — contact emails (polite pools / required by terms).
#    NOT secrets, but required for good standing. (M2-01)
# =========================================================================
# OpenAlex: the mailto "polite pool" was REMOVED in Feb 2026 and mailto is now
# ignored — OPENALEX_MAILTO is obsolete (kept only so an old .env still loads).
OPENALEX_MAILTO=
# Crossref "polite pool": contact email sent as mailto. No API key.
CROSSREF_MAILTO=
# Unpaywall: REQUIRES a contact email as the `email` query param.
UNPAYWALL_EMAIL=

# =========================================================================
# 3. Source APIs — keys. (M2-01)
# =========================================================================
# OpenAlex: key OPTIONAL (keyless works; a free key raises rate limits ~10x,
# sent as the `api_key` query param). This replaces the old mailto polite pool.
OPENALEX_API_KEY=
# CORE (core.ac.uk): API key required for the v3 API.
CORE_API_KEY=
# Semantic Scholar: key OPTIONAL (raises rate limits); works keyless, slower.
SEMANTIC_SCHOLAR_API_KEY=
# DOAJ: reads work without a key; key only for authenticated endpoints.
DOAJ_API_KEY=
# ERIC (eric.ed.gov): public API, no key needed.
# arXiv: public API, no key needed.
# НБУВ / Scopus / WoS / Google Scholar: manual export only, no API key.
# Retraction Watch / Crossref Labs: data download under terms, no key.

# =========================================================================
# 4. Paid LLM providers — DISABLED by default (H9 / ADR-017 / ADR-021).
#    Filling a key does NOT enable paid calls. Enabling needs the budget
#    gate: budget.yaml -> paid_calls: enabled, enabled_by: <approval_id>,
#    plus an external_requests / cost limit. The cost-guard checks before
#    every call. (M3-01, M3-17, external_quality_critic role.)
# =========================================================================
# OpenAI / ChatGPT — external quality validator (ADR-021) and Codex critic
# (M3-17). Core never imports `openai`; it is used only in harness/host/.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Optional OpenAI scoping (leave blank unless you need them):
OPENAI_ORG_ID=
OPENAI_PROJECT_ID=
# Optional base-URL override (self-host / proxy); default is OpenAI's.
OPENAI_BASE_URL=
# NOTE: Anthropic / Claude is the HOST (Claude Code) and uses its own CLI
#   auth — no ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is needed here.
